  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "final-note",
      "page": "final",
      "x": 1000,
      "y": 1400,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "Final direction. Tool cards expand in place for options, General is a second view inside the same panel with a back chevron. Menubar icon has three states: idle, listening (tiny meter), recording (red timer). Tokens are in design/DESIGN.md."
    },
    {
      "id": "v2-note",
      "page": "v2",
      "x": 1280,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "Round 2. Geist only, no serif. Bar meters instead of curves. Recent rows use a tile per item: mic tile for a transcript, thumbnail for a recording. Amber accent throughout; only the ground (background, panel, card, text tint) changes between artboards."
    },
    {
      "id": "concept-note",
      "page": "concept",
      "x": 1240,
      "y": 660,
      "w": 280,
      "text": "Ink and amber, custom chrome. The panel is the whole app: tool cards expand in place for options, so there is no Settings window. Keycaps show the shortcut. The pill grows into a card while transcribing so you see words land before the paste."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-a",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 800,
      "text": "A · Ink and amber. Warm near-black, one amber accent, serif for titles only. Feels like a crafted tool, ages well. Tradeoff: amber on dark is low-contrast for small secondary text, and the serif can read as precious if overused."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-b",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": 900,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 800,
      "text": "B · Glass. Deep indigo ground, frosted layers, periwinkle accent, large radii. Most 'modern' and most in step with current macOS. Tradeoff: blur and translucency are expensive to get right in AppKit, and it dates fastest."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-c",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1780,
      "w": 800,
      "text": "C · Paper. Light, warm off-white, one coral accent, dark pill for contrast. Friendliest and most sellable to non-developers. Tradeoff: light-first means you design dark mode second, and it is the least 'yours' at a glance."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-d",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 1780,
      "w": 800,
      "text": "D · Terminal. Green-black, lime accent, mono for labels, tight radii. Unmistakably a developer tool, dense and fast. Tradeoff: narrowest audience, and lime as the only accent leaves no room for status colours."
    },
    {
      "id": "scope-note",
      "page": "v1",
      "x": 1120,
      "y": 190,
      "w": 260,
      "text": "v1 surfaces only. Dark appearance drawn; light follows system automatically in the real app. No onboarding, no library window, no General pane yet."
    },
    {
      "id": "tabs-note",
      "page": "tabs",
      "x": 1740,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "Tabs direction, 2026-09-15\n\nOne tool visible at a time, so the panel height no longer depends on how many tools exist. The switcher reuses the picker's segment style.\n\nA capturing tool gets a pink dot on its tab and the panel jumps to it when the capture starts.\n\nRecent collapses to one line while a tool's Options are open.\n\nGeneral stays in the footer. Past four tools the switcher goes icon-only; the selected tab keeps its name.\n\nOpen question: drop the title row inside the card, since the tab already names the tool?"
    },
    {
      "id": "list-note",
      "page": "list",
      "x": 1740,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "List and tool views, 2026-09-15\n\nMain view lists every tool as a 52 pt row: tile, name, one-line status, shortcut, chevron. Eight tools fit with room for Recent; the rows are the glanceable state.\n\nA row opens the tool's view (same navigation as General): back chevron, the card with meter and chips, options always open. No accordion, height bounded by one tool.\n\nA capturing tool's row takes the amber (listening) or pink (recording) treatment; the pill carries the live state.\n\nRecent and the footer stay on the main view."
    },
    {
      "id": "history-note",
      "page": "history",
      "x": 1160,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "History view, 2026-09-15\n\nThe main view keeps the last 5 under Recent. Its header gains 'All 48 ›', which pushes the History view (same navigation as General and the tool views).\n\nHistory: search over transcripts and file names, All / Voice / Recordings filter, rows grouped by day with clock times instead of relative ones. The list scrolls inside the panel; 'Show older' loads the next batch.\n\nHover on a row reveals delete next to the copy or reveal action. Delete removes the log row, never the file.\n\nStill one panel, no library window."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "history"
  }
